; DOMAIN: statistical-physics/stochastic-thermodynamics [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-26]
; Claim: For a system driven out of equilibrium by a protocol lambda(t), the work W is a fluctuating quantity obeying exact identities regardless of driving speed. Jarzynski: <e^{-beta W}>=e^{-beta DeltaF}, so the equilibrium free-energy difference DeltaF is recoverable from nonequilibrium work averages; Jensen then gives <W>>=DeltaF (the second law as a convexity bound). Crooks: P_F(W)/P_R(-W)=e^{beta(W-DeltaF)} relates forward/reverse protocol work distributions and implies Jarzynski by integration. The total entropy production Sigma>=0 (system + bath) is the fundamental fluctuating dissipation; its distribution satisfies the detailed fluctuation theorem P(Sigma)/P(-Sigma)=e^{Sigma}, and at large deviations its rate function obeys the Gallavotti-Cohen symmetry I(-sigma)=I(sigma)-sigma. Averaging recovers <Sigma>>=0: the second law is the mean of a fluctuation-theorem-constrained LDP whose negative-entropy-production events are exponentially rare but real.
; Structure: (fluctuating work W under protocol lambda(t)) (Jarzynski <e^{-beta W}>=e^{-beta DeltaF}) (Jensen => <W>>=DeltaF second law) (Crooks P_F(W)/P_R(-W)=e^{beta(W-DeltaF)}) (entropy production Sigma>=0, detailed FT P(Sigma)/P(-Sigma)=e^{Sigma}) (LDP rate Gallavotti-Cohen I(-sigma)=I(sigma)-sigma) (<Sigma>>=0 = mean of FT-constrained rate).
; Result: The second law is not an inequality imposed from outside but the ensemble average of an exact fluctuation symmetry: entropy production is a large-deviation observable whose rate function is pinned by the Gallavotti-Cohen relation, and free energy is an exponential (tilted) average of nonequilibrium work. Thermodynamic irreversibility, MaxEnt free energy, and large-deviation rate functions are one structure — the entropic cost of a trajectory equals its log-probability asymmetry under time reversal.
; Bridge: genesis_large_deviations (entropy production is a large-deviation observable P(Sigma_n approx n*sigma)~exp(-n I(sigma)); the Gallavotti-Cohen symmetry I(-sigma)=I(sigma)-sigma is a fluctuation-theorem constraint on the LDP rate function, and Jarzynski/Crooks are tilted-average / Legendre-dual statements of exactly the Sanov-Cramer entropic structure) + genesis_thermodynamics_maxent (DeltaF is the MaxEnt/Gibbs free-energy difference recovered by the Jarzynski exponential-work average; the tilt e^{-beta W} is the same Gibbs weighting, beta the inverse-temperature Lagrange multiplier) + genesis_entropy_dynamics (the detailed fluctuation theorem is the trajectory-level microscopic origin of the monotone macroscopic entropy increase: <Sigma>>=0 is the coarse-grained arrow of time whose fine-grained content is time-reversal probability asymmetry).